1
00:00:01,010 --> 00:00:03,840
JEONG MIN JUN, Kasper, NaiN, and BABYZOO...

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:07,050
have made it to the Last Stage: 24H.

3
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:10,720
The only condition given for the Last Stage is the Cube.

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,820
(20 Cubes)

5
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:13,250
Wow, this is going to be so much fun.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,650
Within 24 hours...

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,960
- That is just ridiculous.
- I couldn't make the choreography.

8
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,620
Last Stage is a game.

9
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,630
I'll show just how scary someone with nothing to lose can be.

10
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:22,390
I will go in with a do-or-die mindset.

11
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,430
BABYZOO went crazy and...

12
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:27,900
- He went crazy with waacking.
- Just shut it.

13
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,030
It is not easy for the Last Stage to be this exciting.

14
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,540
That can never be produced within 24 hours.

15
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,240
The Stories feels like the Grim Reaper.

16
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:35,940
Let us kill them.

17
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,980
A performance that perfectly hits the spot with the mood you like.

18
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,910
I want to prove myself and show you.

19
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:43,450
But Kasper used the Cube the best.

20
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:44,580
He is built for the Last Stage.

21
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:48,390
How to use the Cube is most important.

22
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:50,720
Do more for the directing.

23
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:54,830
- This is a directors' war.
- Who will be the one eliminated...

24
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:56,930
and leave this stage today?

25
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,700
The Last Stage is truly crazy.

26
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,370
(The second Last Stage with survival on the line begins.)

27
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:01,370
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

28
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:13,410
(Last Stage: 24H)

29
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:17,480
A survival competition with the director's name on the line,

30
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,620
Last Stage: 24H.

31
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:26,490
Today, another Last Stage for survival begins.

32
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,990
(The final gateway to survival, Last Stage: 24H)

33
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,730
(Last Stage: 24H)

34
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:36,700
The only condition given for this Last Stage is the Cube.

35
00:01:37,370 --> 00:01:38,900
(20 Cubes)

36
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:46,040
The Cube is the simplest shape, but on stage,

37
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:48,710
it becomes an "objet" with infinite possibilities.

38
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:53,280
Stack them into a structure. Attach them to make a wall.

39
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:55,920
Arrange them into a space,

40
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:59,220
and with dance, make a masterpiece.

41
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:02,890
Depending on how you utilize the same 20 Cubes,

42
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:04,400
the same stage can be completed...

43
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,900
as a completely different masterpiece.

44
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:11,970
There are a total of four directors facing the Cube of destiny today.

45
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:13,910
(Last Stage: 24H)

46
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:21,350
From battles to choreography, and directing,

47
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:24,580
the all-rounder who crosses genres, Director BABYZOO.

48
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:27,750
Since this could be my last scene in Street World Fighter,

49
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:29,650
I just gritted my teeth and prepared.

50
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,790
I have to show them.

51
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:35,460
The MZ Director leading the new wave of K-pop performance, NaiN.

52
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:37,230
I'm a scary person.

53
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,730
I think I need to cause a major upheaval.

54
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,600
I'm fully confident I can win. I have to win.

55
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,670
(I have to win.)

56
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:46,040
Encompassing both groups and solos,

57
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,610
the director who has set the standard for K-pop performance,

58
00:02:48,610 --> 00:02:49,640
Kasper.

59
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:51,980
Wow, it makes no sense if I lose here.

60
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:55,810
I will win this at all costs for my survival.

61
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,080
The next-generation rising director...

62
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:01,220
who reached the top of a global competition, JEONG MIN JUN.

63
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,120
Since I have experience with the Last Stage,

64
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:05,820
I thought this would be easy to win.

65
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:07,990
It would be harder to get eliminated.

66
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:09,430
I was really confident.

67
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:12,530
Who will be the one director whose directing on this stage...

68
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,970
will be their very last?

69
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:17,900
Prove yourself within 24 hours.

70
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:22,010
The story of those fierce 24 hours starts now.

71
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:32,080
It makes no sense.

72
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:33,320
Is this right?

73
00:03:33,850 --> 00:03:35,250
I couldn't really accept it.

74
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,620
Going to the Last Stage twice is just really infuriating.

75
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:42,260
Actually, I was only thinking about the mission results, but anyway,

76
00:03:42,330 --> 00:03:45,700
it hit me that one of these four is definitely going.

77
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:46,830
This is a nightmare.

78
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:50,030
Their expressions were so stiff...

79
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,870
I felt really weird.

80
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:58,080
I felt sorry for MIN JUN, somehow. It feels like my fault...

81
00:03:58,410 --> 00:03:59,810
- I think I felt a little more...
- Thank you.

82
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:00,880
sorry for NaiN.

83
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:05,120
If I had done a little better, this might not have happened.

84
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:10,820
The Last Stage was just so shocking, really.

85
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:11,890
The Last Stage?

86
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,930
You must be completely losing your mind right now.

87
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:15,830
I cannot get my mind straight right now either.

88
00:04:15,890 --> 00:04:17,630
I cannot think of anything right now.

89
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,530
I really didn't think about it at all.

90
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,300
- I had no time to...
- Me too.

91
00:04:22,370 --> 00:04:24,500
We are all in the same boat.

92
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,840
What should I do, really?

93
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:27,910
(After the results are announced,)

94
00:04:27,910 --> 00:04:29,070
(the four return to the Directors' Room.)

95
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,210
What in the world is happening?

96
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,810
(A heart that just will not calm down)

97
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:36,680
How did we lose?

98
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:39,420
I was so confident.

99
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,250
I think he knows my style.

100
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:43,920
Because I was so certain.

101
00:04:43,990 --> 00:04:45,760
Because it was a well-founded certainty.

102
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:50,400
I just thought it was completely mine.

103
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:52,800
(Bailey's final choice, Simeez and INGYOO.)

104
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,470
I thought I knew Bailey the best, but my judgment was wrong.

105
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:58,240
That was the biggest shock.

106
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,610
While filming this, it was the most...

107
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:04,540
mentally shaking, devastating moment for me.

108
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:07,150
Nothing comes to mind.

109
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:14,290
But the fact that MIN JUN is going twice bothers me...

110
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:17,320
because it feels like I'm sending him off with my own hands.

111
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:19,120
You worked hard.

112
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:22,290
- Man... I'm sorry...
- No.

113
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,260
It is nobody's fault,

114
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,530
- While taking it out like this...
- We worked really hard,

115
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,740
but we just got mixed results.

116
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,670
However, even if I went back,

117
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,270
I think I would've made the same choice.

118
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:37,480
I think I would have made the choice...

119
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,210
to show Bailey doing really well.

120
00:05:41,410 --> 00:05:44,120
So, I ended up going to the Last Stage twice.

121
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:47,020
It is just hardship after hardship after hardship.

122
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:49,690
That is why my mind is blowing up even more.

123
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,590
(BABYZOO's Director's Room is filled with sighs.)

124
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:55,990
I worked really hard.

125
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:59,160
It kind of feels like I'm being completely denied.

126
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:03,840
A project I've poured my heart into failed anyway, right?

127
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,840
I don't have any kids, but it feels like...

128
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:10,110
I have to let my child go, honestly.

129
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:14,680
Since I feel like I failed, it really breaks my heart.

130
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:16,510
But, gosh...

131
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,250
(Sniffling)

132
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,320
This makes no sense.

133
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:26,090
(Sighing)

134
00:06:26,390 --> 00:06:28,660
(NaiN sheds tears over the unexpected result.)

135
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:30,330
How did we lose?

136
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,400
My blood is boiling.

137
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:36,870
It's not easy to be so confident in your work.

138
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:40,810
Seeing the performance that day made me even more confident.

139
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:42,170
I think we definitely have an impact.

140
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:44,180
Our choreography fits better.

141
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,280
I was so sure of that,

142
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:48,050
but it didn't, so it was really, really...

143
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:50,050
the most shocking thing recently.

144
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,020
PD, I really don't have any confidence. What should I do?

145
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,620
No, you can do it, NaiN. Seriously.

146
00:06:55,690 --> 00:06:58,060
PD, I really can't do this...

147
00:06:58,590 --> 00:06:59,920
No, you can do it.

148
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:05,200
I didn't think of the Last Stage because I didn't think I would.

149
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:07,670
One out of these four is eliminated?

150
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:10,640
But if it's me, it really won't work out.

151
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,270
It really won't work out, you know?

152
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,940
- It can't be...
- I can't...

153
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:15,510
(Thud)

154
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:16,710
If you say that...

155
00:07:18,410 --> 00:07:21,180
- Will I be able to make it up?
- You can do it.

156
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:24,120
NaiN, you worked so hard.

157
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,750
You worked hard too.

158
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,690
- Goodness.
- Good job.

159
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,790
We don't have time to get caught up...

160
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:34,030
in all these emotions right now,

161
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:35,490
so first, let's just do it...

162
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:37,530
and unwind after the Last Stage is over.

163
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,060
We have to.

164
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:40,970
I just wanted to say you worked really hard.

165
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:43,030
NaiN, so I thought about it like this.

166
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,370
We get to show one more performance.

167
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:48,540
Just like, hey, isn't this a forced Lucky Vicky?

168
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:50,070
The two of us are moving up.

169
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:51,480
Yes. Definitely.

170
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:55,650
He kept cheering me on, so I felt incredibly grateful.

171
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,650
So I gritted my teeth even more...

172
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:00,790
and decided to pour everything into this.

173
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,720
I had to accept it quickly...

174
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,160
I decided to do my best.

175
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:10,460
But I didn't want to feel disappointed during that time.

176
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:14,670
I'm really going to treat the Last Stage as just a game.

177
00:08:15,030 --> 00:08:17,000
The situation is already set, we have to solve it,

178
00:08:17,070 --> 00:08:19,500
and time is ticking, so what else can we do but do it?

179
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:22,470
We have no choice. But what's bothering me is,

180
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:25,740
how can we use that Objet creatively?

181
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:27,910
How is everyone going to use that?

182
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,950
The condition for this Last Stage is right...

183
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:33,050
- There's a condition?
- inside this Director's Room.

184
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:35,850
- Where? A condition?
- Are we supposed to find it?

185
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,260
Like "Running Man" or something? Is it hidden somewhere?

186
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:42,260
Is it that?

187
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:45,700
It is that. That box right there.

188
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:49,030
Oh, this box. Okay. The Cube. With the Cube, with this box...

189
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:51,900
What exactly am I supposed to do? This is driving me crazy. Okay.

190
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,470
Just one?

191
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:55,910
You must use a total of 20 Cubes...

192
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,740
to complete your performance.

193
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,640
What? 20 Cubes?

194
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:01,250
I have already been through this once.

195
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:02,650
When it comes to utilizing the Objet...

196
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:04,480
I think I have the biggest advantage since I have experience.

197
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:08,850
Because I already know exactly what the Last Stage demands from us.

198
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,260
Honestly, the people who will be at the biggest disadvantage are...

199
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,520
everyone except me?

200
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,360
20 Cubes...

201
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,160
It is very shocking in many ways.

202
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:19,860
Still, I think I need to be as strategic as possible about this.

203
00:09:19,930 --> 00:09:23,970
I think I need to bring out the secret weapon that I'm best at.

204
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,770
The Cubes are all separated,

205
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,740
and I can make whatever shape I want with them,

206
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,270
so I just have to make it happen.

207
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:33,340
First of all, I must work hard and not let my guard down.

208
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:35,180
Doing my best and working hard is a given,

209
00:09:35,250 --> 00:09:36,450
but I also have to do well.

210
00:09:36,510 --> 00:09:37,780
Those who are willing to die will live,

211
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:39,450
and those who only want to survive will die.

212
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:41,550
I'm going into this with a do-or-die mindset.

213
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:43,890
I will fight tooth and nail to survive this time too.

214
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,320
(Last Stage: 24H, Music and Outfit Concept)

215
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:51,160
I actually brought a sound that I can dance really well to.

216
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:53,970
I think I need to use my ultimate move for this Last Stage.

217
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:56,170
The kind of power that only waacking can show.

218
00:09:56,230 --> 00:09:58,340
I have been doing this for seven or eight years anyway,

219
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:00,540
so my personal style is distinct. It is my own style.

220
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,770
I was confident that

221
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:03,770
layering different sounds over string instruments...

222
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,940
would create something really cool.

223
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:07,980
For the outfit, I wanted to take things back to the past.

224
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:09,580
I wore pants made of the kind...

225
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:14,250
of dance sports dancers wear when I used to be a waacking dancer.

226
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:19,860
I think we went with neat, polished hair and makeup to match.

227
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,560
It's funky,

228
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:25,760
but it's not just rhythmical, it has really punchy sources.

229
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:29,070
The genre is close to New Jack Swing.

230
00:10:29,370 --> 00:10:32,500
It's got a lot of funk and similar vibes.

231
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:36,710
Whenever I have to prepare a stage for a survival show or competition,

232
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:40,640
I tend to choose serious, intense music.

233
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:46,250
But this time, I wanted to just be happy and dance.

234
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,290
Out of the four teams, our outfits are the only ones...

235
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:50,790
that are super flashy, right?

236
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:52,390
I matched our ties and accessories,

237
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:54,330
but I used a variety of colors...

238
00:10:54,330 --> 00:10:56,460
because I wanted to give off a free-spirited vibe.

239
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:58,760
The only team I'm keeping my eye on is MIN JUN.

240
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:02,100
MIN JUN has already been through this, so I think he will do well.

241
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:05,770
- He knows exactly what to expect.
- That is right.

242
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:08,870
Since I have been to the abyss and back,

243
00:11:10,070 --> 00:11:11,880
I prepared a priest outfit.

244
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,940
I'm not worried about the Last Stage.

245
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:16,750
The formula I'm good at in competitions is...

246
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,880
I hook them in during the intro,

247
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,120
then connect the technical elements...

248
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,750
after hitting them with a wow factor,

249
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:23,850
and finish by driving it home at the end.

250
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:25,260
I was really confident in that.

251
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,760
I had to build it from scratch to fit the mood of the track.

252
00:11:27,830 --> 00:11:31,160
- Yes.
- I want it to hit hard.

253
00:11:31,230 --> 00:11:32,460
As a person,

254
00:11:32,530 --> 00:11:34,670
I come off as someone who would do contemporary dance,

255
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:37,270
and my music is usually very lyrical,

256
00:11:37,270 --> 00:11:40,100
so this time, I wanted to use something I like...

257
00:11:40,170 --> 00:11:42,340
and try dancing to hip-hop music.

258
00:11:43,410 --> 00:11:47,680
I definitely want to stand out among the four of us.

259
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,250
I'm going to create a new picture.

260
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:52,480
I wanted to try making some intense EDM music.

261
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:54,150
Since I'm not just going to dance,

262
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,150
I want to keep making things explode.

263
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:58,360
I have been obsessed with EDM music since last year.

264
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:00,490
It is not very popular in Korea yet,

265
00:12:00,490 --> 00:12:03,860
but I wanted to make UK Bass genre EDM music.

266
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,100
I like that music.

267
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,770
Whether it's Coachella or Lollapalooza...

268
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:10,270
When I go there,

269
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:12,100
everyone is wearing sunglasses...

270
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,110
There are a lot of stylish people with that edgy, metallic look...

271
00:12:14,110 --> 00:12:15,540
people talk about.

272
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,110
To match that music,

273
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:21,750
I wanted to use something that was Matrix-like...

274
00:12:22,550 --> 00:12:23,610
with a cybernetic feel.

275
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:26,880
And the key point was the laser. It was my secret weapon.

276
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:29,290
I just have to prepare for the Last Stage.

277
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:30,520
I have to keep proving myself.

278
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,360
Proving myself in here seems to be my role.

279
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,530
(Team NaiN's Practice Room)

280
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,530
(Crashing)

281
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:43,330
The Cubes are coming.

282
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:45,940
So this is what it feels like.

283
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,910
Wait, we're not just choreographing,

284
00:12:48,970 --> 00:12:50,410
we're using physical strength too?

285
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:52,810
(The 20 cubes delivered to NaiN's practice room.)

286
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:55,350
The Cubes just came pouring in.

287
00:12:55,410 --> 00:12:58,450
Honestly, in my dictionary, there was no Last Stage,

288
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,550
so I intentionally didn't think about the Cubes.

289
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:05,960
Preparing for the Last Stage and looking at Cubes overwhelmed me.

290
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,030
The Cubes are surprisingly heavy.

291
00:13:08,230 --> 00:13:10,390
They were so heavy, and even before choreographing,

292
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:13,460
I lost all my strength and my hands hurt.

293
00:13:13,530 --> 00:13:15,970
So I put on red work gloves by myself...

294
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,840
and moved the Cubes for several hours.

295
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,840
(Channeling the power of work gloves)

296
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,910
I feel like this is a reality check.

297
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:29,980
I didn't know where to start, thinking, "What do I do?"

298
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,450
I just stared at the Cubes for a few hours.

299
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:37,960
I took notes and did that for six to seven hours.

300
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:41,160
Touching them, moving them, making shapes...

301
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:45,330
or making stairs, this and that, I imagined everything.

302
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:51,770
Just standing them up seemed like underutilizing them,

303
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,870
so together with our formation and dance,

304
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:56,270
so they can look blended in,

305
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:58,740
I kept trying to use them like that without resting.

306
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:02,780
Not just leaving the Cubes standing, but together with our dance,

307
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:05,620
I strategized with the goal of moving them and doing it together.

308
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:10,350
I mean, others might do even more, so I'm scared.

309
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,720
Everyone probably did something amazing.

310
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:13,620
No, no, from what I see, no one used them to this extent.

311
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,160
MIN JUN probably used them amazingly.

312
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:16,460
MIN JUN did use them amazingly.

313
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:19,830
MIN JUN, in the previous Last Stage, did so well, so...

314
00:14:20,630 --> 00:14:22,770
I should flip this over and turn it into a boat.

315
00:14:22,830 --> 00:14:26,670
I figured nobody else would have even thought of flipping the desk.

316
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,640
So I was not worried.

317
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:32,710
(JEONG MIN JUN's Practice Room)

318
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:37,180
(Dangling, Flailing)

319
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:40,280
(Before utilizing the cubes, MIN JUN utilizes his body first.)

320
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:42,490
If someone holds this box from behind,

321
00:14:42,550 --> 00:14:44,590
when I hit it, it flies back and...

322
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:45,890
Like this kind of image...

323
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:48,860
- We doing another tough concept?
- Kind of?

324
00:14:50,030 --> 00:14:52,260
Honestly, last time, as soon as I saw the Objet,

325
00:14:52,330 --> 00:14:53,600
I thought, "I should flip it and make a boat."

326
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:54,930
The idea just came to me right away.

327
00:14:55,030 --> 00:14:57,400
But this time, I had no idea how to use the Cube.

328
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:59,770
I went in without being able to even imagine what to do.

329
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:01,340
There was nothing I could do.

330
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:05,140
I didn't even have a sense of direction. Not even a guideline.

331
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,280
Is there anything you want to do?

332
00:15:08,350 --> 00:15:10,480
Like last time, "I'm going to make a boat."

333
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:12,950
- Honestly, I have not decided yet.
- Okay.

334
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:14,620
(Climbing Up)

335
00:15:14,690 --> 00:15:15,690
(Jumping Over)

336
00:15:15,750 --> 00:15:17,320
I could jump over it like parkour.

337
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:18,760
Something like this...

338
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:23,660
The important thing about the Last Stage Objet is not just using it,

339
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:26,560
but having a reason for it. There has to be a purpose behind it.

340
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:29,170
So maybe I could show who I really am?

341
00:15:29,230 --> 00:15:31,370
Since this is my second time on Last Stage,

342
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:34,670
I felt a sense of desperation. A desire to survive.

343
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:37,680
Thinking of myself now as if I were out in the wilderness,

344
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,680
I designed the performance around...

345
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,750
the theme "Through the Wilderness."

346
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:44,050
To convey that kind of idea easily,

347
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:47,080
I wanted to choose a theme that...

348
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,090
people could immediately understand intuitively.

349
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:53,690
So what if we just flip this over like this?

350
00:15:53,690 --> 00:15:54,790
(Flipped over)

351
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:56,290
We have black tape, right?

352
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:57,860
Oh. With tape, just like this...

353
00:15:57,930 --> 00:15:59,930
There was non-woven fabric on it,

354
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:02,270
but to visually depict the image of a "road,"

355
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:06,370
I just peeled off all the fabric and put black tape on top.

356
00:16:06,370 --> 00:16:08,010
It's too short.

357
00:16:08,010 --> 00:16:10,210
Oh, try it. Try it.

358
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:16,680
As you pass through the wilderness, a road appears.

359
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,180
A road emerges.

360
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:22,650
And so, if people dance on this road and just move sideways,

361
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:24,320
you would think, "Wow, they are traveling down a road."

362
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,790
That is what comes to mind.

363
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:30,590
Since the concept and Objet usage got the most feedback before,

364
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,160
how well you use the Objet...

365
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,870
Those two are the biggest factors.

366
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,070
Let me give it a go.

367
00:16:36,070 --> 00:16:38,800
Since I'm the only one who knows this,

368
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:41,370
I think I have the advantage.

369
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:44,010
Get ready to be amazed.

370
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:45,340
Look forward to it.

371
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:48,750
(Team BABYZOO's Practice Room)

372
00:16:48,950 --> 00:16:51,650
(BABYZOO checks the cube as soon as he arrives.)

373
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,690
The weight was the most important thing.

374
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:56,350
We had to do something by pushing them.

375
00:16:56,350 --> 00:17:01,390
Or the cubes are connected, and then they open together.

376
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,690
Or they change positions.

377
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:07,260
The thought of being trapped between the cubes came to mind.

378
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,100
I absolutely had to do that.

379
00:17:10,230 --> 00:17:14,870
Start. And one, two, three, and four,

380
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:16,840
five, and six.

381
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:19,680
(Practice interrupted by the time spent moving the cubes.)

382
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,550
Is it too hard? Are you okay?

383
00:17:21,550 --> 00:17:23,050
- It's okay.
- Yes. Tell me if it is too much.

384
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:26,980
(Practice resumes once again.)

385
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:31,020
Push slowly, keep pushing.

386
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,790
(Startled)

387
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:36,160
- Okay, Do Yun, are you okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

388
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,300
- I missed the handle by mistake.
- That's okay.

389
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,400
(The more they practice, the more moving mishaps keep happening.)

390
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:44,000
That is it. Careful, careful.

391
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,470
But I was worried this might be too much,

392
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:47,540
so if it is too hard, please tell me.

393
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,010
Because our only practice time is tomorrow...

394
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:50,510
and today, that is all we have left.

395
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,240
The most important point was that...

396
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,750
the cubes were heavier than expected.

397
00:17:55,750 --> 00:17:59,020
Since they are girls, the strength to hold on and push through...

398
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:00,220
- is a lot weaker.
- Again.

399
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:02,190
So if we were not careful,

400
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:04,290
there were a few things I decided just would not work.

401
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,620
I think that was the case.

402
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:07,160
Oh, this is driving me crazy.

403
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,760
It is so hard, seriously. It is not easy at all.

404
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:15,100
It is really so hard. So hard.

405
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:19,900
I was exhausted too, dizzy and everything,

406
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,710
but I should have made a judgment call right there.

407
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:25,340
Again.

408
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:29,380
But still, from that point on, we have to fill in what is lacking.

409
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:30,780
Okay, slowly.

410
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:33,180
From now on, we have nothing to lose.

411
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:36,150
I will show you how dangerous someone with nothing to lose can be.

412
00:18:37,650 --> 00:18:39,760
(Team Kasper's Practice Room)

413
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:44,060
(Kasper begins practice)

414
00:18:45,130 --> 00:18:46,130
(Swoosh)

415
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:51,670
I said if it was the Last Stage, I would rather jump in the ocean.

416
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,040
That is how badly I didn't want to go to the Last Stage.

417
00:18:54,770 --> 00:18:55,870
(Sighing)

418
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,270
What am I supposed to do with this?

419
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,280
What exactly are they telling me to do?

420
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:01,480
I never imagined I would have 20 Cubes sitting right in front of me.

421
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:03,750
Darn it. I have no idea what to do.

422
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:08,290
First of all, they are way too heavy,

423
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:09,690
and there is nothing we can do with them.

424
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:11,020
I'm just going home.

425
00:19:11,090 --> 00:19:13,420
There is nothing you can do with these.

426
00:19:13,490 --> 00:19:14,490
Come on.

427
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:17,090
(A sigh grows as the cubes keep piling up.)

428
00:19:17,230 --> 00:19:18,560
How many people do we need?

429
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:19,700
What was the Production Team thinking...

430
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:21,670
preparing something like this?

431
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:23,400
So we just use these Cubes...

432
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:25,740
- however we can, right?
- Right.

433
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:30,240
(With the Cubes just stacked up, time passes mercilessly.)

434
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:32,980
Let us take this out and try pushing four of them together like this.

435
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,680
Stick them together, like this.

436
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:38,420
I wanted to build a structure and kept thinking about...

437
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,650
what kind of movements we could do with the Cubes.

438
00:19:42,650 --> 00:19:44,020
I didn't want to use them in a simple way.

439
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:46,520
I didn't want us to just stand there dancing.

440
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:50,830
(He begins unpacking the ideas in his head one by one.)

441
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:54,330
One, two, three... One more person comes here...

442
00:19:54,830 --> 00:19:57,900
Four, five, six.

443
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:00,240
and builds this.

444
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:06,940
Either way, matching the keyword "pressure,"

445
00:20:07,010 --> 00:20:09,550
controlling and moving the Cubes.

446
00:20:09,550 --> 00:20:10,610
Darn it.

447
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:13,820
I have been thinking about doing something like this...

448
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:15,220
- That's good.
- No way!

449
00:20:15,390 --> 00:20:16,420
(Surprised)

450
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:18,290
(Applause, amazed)

451
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:20,090
I'll do this.

452
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:21,690
That is what I thought.

453
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,160
It would be good if it looked fascinating.

454
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,230
Six, seven.

455
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:27,200
(Kasper's Ideas are gaining momentum)

456
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:28,500
Out of everything we have seen so far,

457
00:20:28,570 --> 00:20:29,900
that was the best.

458
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:31,340
I think this will work.

459
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:33,540
(Last Stage: 24H, D-Day)

460
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,940
Just thinking about it is really scary.

461
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:38,480
(Waiting room for the four surviving choreographers)

462
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:39,680
Are two people going to stand up next?

463
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,310
Before this, for the Last Stage,

464
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:42,680
we just assumed we would be eliminated.

465
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:44,080
Right, right, right.

466
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,450
But this time, it just has to be you.

467
00:20:45,450 --> 00:20:46,850
Right, right, right.

468
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,520
But honestly, during the table mission,

469
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:51,690
I was confident.

470
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:53,090
I thought I could make the tables work somehow.

471
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,590
But I was not confident about the Cube.

472
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:56,860
- The awkwardly rectangular shape...
- Right.

473
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:57,890
seemed difficult.

474
00:20:57,890 --> 00:20:59,360
It looks extremely uncomfortable.

475
00:20:59,430 --> 00:21:01,630
So I think it would have been even harder with 20 Cubes.

476
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:03,770
Since MIN JUN made it back alive,

477
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,570
I'm curious about what he did this time.

478
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:08,670
Second Last Stage run-through will now begin.

479
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:10,240
It does feel like there are a lot of people today.

480
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:11,380
- Because of multiple teams.
- Four teams.

481
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,380
You're right.

482
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:13,880
(NaiN 25, Kasper 25, BABYZOO 24, MIN JUN 12)

483
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:16,180
Wow, but MIN JUN's team is a small group again.

484
00:21:16,250 --> 00:21:17,550
I think they only have three crews.

485
00:21:17,950 --> 00:21:19,220
The number of people is really almost...

486
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:21,490
- double the amount here.
- How many dancers do you have?

487
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:23,620
We have 25, right?

488
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,620
- We have 12.
- 12?

489
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:29,190
MIN JUN's team has fewer people,

490
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:31,430
so what could they have done? I'm curious.

491
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:33,900
For my Last Mission, the concept and the Objet...

492
00:21:33,900 --> 00:21:34,970
seem to be the most important.

493
00:21:35,030 --> 00:21:36,570
I have experience with the Last Stage,

494
00:21:36,630 --> 00:21:37,670
so I'm confident.

495
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,970
Kasper must be doing the Matrix.

496
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,270
They are the only ones wearing gloves right now.

497
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,970
They are even wearing sunglasses.

498
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,440
I think they are going for a strong vibe.

499
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:46,580
- Exactly.
- Wow, look at BABYZOO's team.

500
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:48,180
Wow, it is crazy, it is crazy.

501
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:50,280
I know, it looks like a competition. Those are combat uniforms.

502
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,880
They are all waackers.

503
00:21:51,950 --> 00:21:53,220
That is a weapon. That is BABYZOO's weapon.

504
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,280
BABYZOO is going to show us today.

505
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:55,390
He has to show us.

506
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:56,520
The Cubes are here.

507
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,890
What are they doing? What are they doing with that?

508
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:01,860
- NaiN?
- NaiN's team is number one.

509
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:03,160
- Let's go!
- Looking at their outfits,

510
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,430
I think they will do something exciting.

511
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,130
Wow, what can they show in 1 minute and 30 seconds? Seriously.

512
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:09,600
Wow, they are making something.

513
00:22:09,670 --> 00:22:11,670
Hey, they are playing with Legos.

514
