01:13:49,830 --> 01:13:51,700
For the casting, through the Kids' Battle...

1545
01:13:51,770 --> 01:13:54,040
- Kids' Battle?
- That sounds fun.

1546
01:13:54,100 --> 01:13:55,240
This is unbelievable.

1547
01:13:56,740 --> 01:13:57,740
(Goosebumps)

1548
01:13:57,940 --> 01:13:59,680
That kid is my one pick.

1549
01:13:59,810 --> 01:14:01,510
Oh, they are just so good.

1550
01:14:01,850 --> 01:14:03,650
(Global super kids' next-level dance skills)

1551
01:14:04,380 --> 01:14:06,180
This kid has a higher hang time for techniques.

1552
01:14:06,250 --> 01:14:07,550
I actually think the opposite.

1553
01:14:07,990 --> 01:14:09,220
Oh, that is so cool.

1554
01:14:09,290 --> 01:14:12,320
- Hino is good.
- Let us pick this kid then.

1555
01:14:12,860 --> 01:14:14,260
Oh, their body is really light.

1556
01:14:15,330 --> 01:14:16,930
(In awe)

1557
01:14:17,590 --> 01:14:18,600
They are so good.

1558
01:14:20,430 --> 01:14:21,500
(Can't believe their eyes)

1559
01:14:23,030 --> 01:14:24,700
Oh, they are really good.

1560
01:14:25,200 --> 01:14:26,670
Wow, this kid is amazing.

1561
01:14:26,740 --> 01:14:29,170
This is crazy.

1562
01:14:29,240 --> 01:14:31,070
We must not lose that kid.

1563
01:14:31,140 --> 01:14:32,880
If we pick this one, I think we will overlap anyway.

1564
01:14:32,880 --> 01:14:33,880
Yes.

1565
01:14:33,940 --> 01:14:35,150
It looks like that team wants this kid too.

1566
01:14:35,480 --> 01:14:36,480
(Spotted Shi.Mi.Zu)

1567
01:14:36,550 --> 01:14:38,780
- Don't look at who we're checking.
- I'm not.

1568
01:14:38,850 --> 01:14:41,790
If two teams select the same kid dancer,

1569
01:14:42,250 --> 01:14:45,590
the final choice will be given to the kid dancer.

1570
01:14:45,720 --> 01:14:46,890
This one.

1571
01:14:46,890 --> 01:14:48,190
(The global kid dancers' choice is the four-person team.)

1572
01:14:48,260 --> 01:14:49,590
I choose here.

1573
01:14:50,260 --> 01:14:52,000
(The global kid dancers' choice is the four-person team times three.)

1574
01:14:52,060 --> 01:14:53,060
(Continuous frustration)

1575
01:14:53,460 --> 01:14:54,830
I guess it is not meant to be for us.

1576
01:14:54,900 --> 01:14:56,170
We do not have the fame right now.

1577
01:14:56,230 --> 01:14:57,870
The kids will unconditionally pick that team.

1578
01:14:57,930 --> 01:14:59,640
What should we do since we're an unpopular team?

1579
01:15:00,040 --> 01:15:03,270
I have never made a choice this carefully before.

1580
01:15:03,340 --> 01:15:06,840
I'm actually very worried. Now, shall we all try it together?

1581
01:15:06,910 --> 01:15:07,910
I cannot do this.

1582
01:15:08,250 --> 01:15:09,410
(The chaotic practice started like that)

1583
01:15:09,650 --> 01:15:10,710
Chaos has arrived.

1584
01:15:10,780 --> 01:15:11,780
Hey, why are you like this?

1585
01:15:11,850 --> 01:15:14,850
Wait a minute, wait a minute. Please wait a minute!

1586
01:15:16,090 --> 01:15:17,490
Oh, I can't do it.

1587
01:15:17,690 --> 01:15:18,720
I can't do it.

1588
01:15:18,720 --> 01:15:20,020
I have completely given up.

1589
01:15:20,560 --> 01:15:23,160
Guys, are you okay? Guys, answer me.

1590
01:15:23,290 --> 01:15:25,700
- Yes.
- Okay. Guys, focus.

1591
01:15:25,760 --> 01:15:28,000
Again. Just this part again.

1592
01:15:28,070 --> 01:15:29,670
Again.

1593
01:15:29,730 --> 01:15:32,400
Tell them if they do not get this right, we must shoot it 100 times.

1594
01:15:33,070 --> 01:15:36,240
(If you can't get this right, you will have to shoot it 100 times.)

1595
01:15:36,340 --> 01:15:39,780
He is basically cracking down on the kids so harshly.

1596
01:15:39,840 --> 01:15:42,780
It didn't look like he had them under control.

1597
01:15:43,250 --> 01:15:45,020
I think the kids follow me the best.

1598
01:15:45,250 --> 01:15:48,090
Director, why do you keep looking at the ground?

1599
01:15:48,090 --> 01:15:49,090
Exactly.

1600
01:15:49,090 --> 01:15:50,390
(Flustered)

1601
01:15:50,450 --> 01:15:52,060
(Laughing)

1602
01:15:52,160 --> 01:15:54,490
- Look into their eyes when dancing.
- Okay.

1603
01:15:54,560 --> 01:15:55,860
Then it would not have been nine to zero.

1604
01:15:56,360 --> 01:15:57,360
(Losing it)

1605
01:15:57,460 --> 01:15:59,130
I will give you one vote.

1606
01:15:59,760 --> 01:16:01,700
Just, if Shuzuki...

1607
01:16:01,770 --> 01:16:05,940
I'm certain that our film will get a good review.

1608
01:16:06,270 --> 01:16:07,670
That's it.

1609
01:16:07,670 --> 01:16:08,940
Focus!

1610
01:16:09,270 --> 01:16:11,410
We have a clear technical advantage.

1611
01:16:11,480 --> 01:16:13,280
I think the quality will be much better.

1612
01:16:13,340 --> 01:16:14,340
Good.

1613
01:16:14,340 --> 01:16:15,350
Let's try it.

1614
01:16:15,750 --> 01:16:17,150
There are four directors...

1615
01:16:17,810 --> 01:16:20,620
for the Super Kids Directing Mission,

1616
01:16:21,490 --> 01:16:22,520
heading to the third Last Stage.

1617
01:16:22,550 --> 01:16:23,790
- What?
- Why?

1618
01:16:23,850 --> 01:16:25,290
Wow, are they leaving three people behind?

1619
01:16:25,360 --> 01:16:26,920
The chances for three people are low.

1620
01:16:27,060 --> 01:16:28,690
I hope the people who have not gone get to go.

1621
01:16:28,760 --> 01:16:30,490
There are exactly four people. Four people who have not gone.

1622
01:16:30,560 --> 01:16:32,930
There will be two choreographers who will leave...

1623
01:16:32,930 --> 01:16:33,930
Directors' War.
